From 07760af4c4e769b815269fe1c84c312b450474a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] ac, radv: work around PS4 GPU and firmware differences

The PS4's system software sets up the GPU differently from the amdgpu
kernel:

- PA_SC_RASTER_CONFIG is set by the system (has_kernel_raster_config).
- CLEAR_STATE leaves garbage in PA_CL_NANINF_CNTL, so it is always
  written on GFX6-9.
- SH_MEM_CONFIG.ALIGNMENT_MODE isn't UNALIGNED, so misaligned typed
  vertex fetches return wrong data (has_unaligned_typed_vtx_fetch).
- The CP hangs on SET_PREDICATION (has_set_predication) and on
  DRAW_(INDEX_)INDIRECT_MULTI (has_draw_indirect_multi), and the CB on
  surfaces with CMASK (has_cmask). Without them, conditional rendering,
  draw indirect count, CMASK and FMASK are not used.
- The GS ring sizes and the tessellation factor ring are owned by the
  system, which ignores the driver's register writes
  (fixed_gs_ring_size, fixed_tess_factor_ring_va).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
